{"claims":[{"excerpt":"The unemployment rate is calculated using the number of unemployed people and the number of employed people—not everyone without a job.","claim":"The unemployment rate uses employed and unemployed people, rather than everyone without a job, as its relevant population.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The unemployment rate divides unemployed people by the sum of employed and unemployed people.","narrative":"Establish that the unemployment rate divides unemployed people by the combined number of employed and unemployed people, rather than by everyone without a job.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The sentence describes the rate’s employed-plus-unemployed population; the ending specifies its denominator.","materiality":"Material to understanding who is included in the rate."},{"excerpt":"To be counted as unemployed, a person generally must have been without work during the reference week","claim":"A person generally must not have been employed during the reference week to be counted as unemployed.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Under the Current Population Survey, an unemployed person was not employed during the survey reference week","narrative":"the person must not have been employed during the reference week","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"“Without work” conveys the source’s “not employed” condition in this context.","materiality":"Material classification condition."},{"excerpt":"available for work","claim":"A person generally must have been available for work to be counted as unemployed.","category":"other","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"was available for work except for temporary illness","narrative":"must have been available for work, except for temporary illness","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The content states the general availability condition and later identifies the temporary-illness exception.","materiality":"Material classification condition."},{"excerpt":"actively searching for a job during the four-week period ending with that week.","claim":"A person generally must have actively searched for work during the four-week period ending with the reference week.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"made an active job search effort in the four-week period ending with that week","narrative":"Active search must fall within the four-week period ending with the reference week","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The stated search activity and period match the source.","materiality":"Material classification condition."},{"excerpt":"A person on temporary layoff who expects to be recalled may qualify without actively searching.","claim":"A person temporarily laid off and expecting recall may qualify without active job search.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"or was temporarily laid off and expected recall","narrative":"A person on temporary layoff who expects recall may qualify without an active search","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This correctly states the temporary-layoff exception to the active-search requirement.","materiality":"Material exception to the general search condition."},{"excerpt":"They must still have been unemployed during the reference week and available for work, with temporary illness as an exception to the availability requirement.","claim":"A temporarily laid-off person must still have been unemployed during the reference week and available for work, except when temporary illness prevents availability.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"an unemployed person was not employed during the survey reference week, was available for work except for temporary illness","narrative":"the person must not have been employed during the reference week and must have been available for work, except for temporary illness","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The content preserves both conditions and the temporary-illness exception.","materiality":"Material limits on the temporary-layoff exception."},{"excerpt":"By contrast, someone whose only job-search activity was browsing listings has not met the active-search requirement.","claim":"Browsing listings alone does not count as active job search.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Passive-only job search does not count as active search.","narrative":"someone whose only job-search activity was browsing listings. ... passive browsing alone does not meet the active-search requirement","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This is consistent with the source’s rule for passive-only search.","materiality":"Material to the contrast between active and passive search."},{"excerpt":"That person would not qualify on that basis alone unless the temporary-layoff exception applies.","claim":"A person whose only search activity was browsing listings does not qualify on that basis alone, unless the temporary-layoff exception applies.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Passive-only job search does not count as active search. ... or was temporarily laid off and expected recall.","narrative":"passive browsing alone does not meet the active-search requirement. The first may qualify without an active search","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The exception is appropriately limited to people temporarily laid off and expecting recall; the sentence does not imply browsing itself qualifies.","materiality":"Material qualification of the passive-search rule."},{"excerpt":"These conditions determine who is classified as unemployed and included alongside employed people in the rate’s denominator.","claim":"The stated conditions determine who is classified as unemployed and counted with employed people in the unemployment-rate denominator.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The unemployment rate divides unemployed people by the sum of employed and unemployed people.","narrative":"Clarify that availability and the survey reference periods also matter, and that the classification determines whether a person is counted among the unemployed in the rate’s denominator.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The sentence accurately links classification to inclusion in the denominator.","materiality":"Material relationship between classification and the rate."}]}

